      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The neighborhood’s name comes from José Brás, a Portuguese farm owner whose land later became the heart of the district.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://saopaulosecreto.com/en/bras-neighborhood-of-sao-paulo/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the 19th century, Brás attracted Italian immigrants who helped shape its bustling garment trade, especially jeans.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://saopaulosecreto.com/en/bras-neighborhood-of-sao-paulo/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The former Hospedaria de Imigrantes do Brás now houses the Immigration Museum, a key spot for learning about the neighborhood’s immigrant history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        27,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
